# (No more OCapN tests skipped — the 7 interop tests previously
# listed here now hard-fail if Node deps are missing rather than
# silently exiting and crashing the batch-worker. Both test.yml
# and interop.yml install Node + npm interop deps.)

# test-ocapn-bridge.rkt — 147 test-cases, each of which elaborates the whole
# OCapN module chain through the shared fixture. ~73s locally but >300s on a
# 2-core GitHub runner: a >4x ratio where the suite overall is ~2.3x, so it is
# disproportionately hurt by 4 batch workers contending on a small box.
#
# Two things were tried first and are recorded so they are not retried:
#   - SPLITTING it in two made CI WORSE (1 timeout -> 2, both halves over the
#     limit). NOT because the per-file cost dominates — that was my first
#     explanation and it is wrong. MEASURED: the shared fixture costs 8.8s
#     (same preamble, one trivial test) and each test ~0.40s, so splitting
#     added ~9s to a >300s file, under 3%. Both halves timed out for a duller
#     reason: half of >300s is still over the 120s limit then in force.
#   - Raising the per-file budget to 300s (the runner now plumbs
#     --file-timeout through to batch-worker.rkt, which is a real gap closed)
#     was still not enough.
#
# What is actually disproportionate is the PER-TEST cost on CI: the suite
# overall runs 2.3x slower there (942s vs 402s) but this file runs >4.4x
# slower (>300s vs 68s), which works out to ~1.9s/test against 0.40s here.
# Ruled out locally, each measured, none reproducing it: CPU contention
# (3 burners on 4 cores, 68.7s vs 67.5s idle), oversubscription (7 burners,
# 67.7s), and cold .pnet caches (all 15 deleted, 63.3s). The remaining
# candidate is runner resources — peak RSS is 497MB per run, so 4 concurrent
# workers want ~2GB, comfortable on this 16GB box and much less so on a
# smaller runner where GC would hit allocation-heavy propagator tests hardest.
# That is a hypothesis; pinning it needs instrumenting the CI job (log peak
# RSS + core count there), not more local runs.
#
# So this is the documented partition case from .claude/rules/testing.md:
# "when test infrastructure mismatches a test's needs, partition rather than
# patch". It runs in full via `raco test` in interop.yml, where it has the
# job's 30-minute budget to itself and no worker contention.
test-ocapn-bridge.rkt  # 147 cases; >300s under batch-worker contention — runs in interop.yml
